.TH INGEST 1 "2026-11-10" "pdp64" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ingest \- read back the answers typed into the pdp64 feedback form
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ingest.py
[\fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-annot\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-annotations\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fB\-\-no\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-deleted\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the edited form (default \fIdocs/feedback/decisions\-feedback.txt\fR; a copy at any path will
do) and prints a Markdown report on standard output.  For each entry that has an answer, a note
or an annotation it shows the parsed DECISION line (letters, "other", "defer" or empty), the
NOTE text (the text after "NOTE:" up to the next entry), and the annotations that fall on its
line range.  It then lists the entries still open and the free text of the section "New
questions and decisions".  It writes \fIanswers.json\fR beside the form and changes no other file.
.PP
A DECISION may be letters separated by commas or spaces ("A, C"), "other: text", "defer", or a
combination; free text that is not a letter list is taken as "other".  A letter the entry did
not offer is reported as not offered.
.PP
Annotations are read from the SQLite database of the pager
(\fI~/.local/share/winless/winless.db\fR, table \fIannotations\fR) for the rows whose file is the
form's absolute path (add names with \fB\-\-annot\-file\fR when the notes were made on another path),
excluding hidden ones.  A selection is matched by its rows (lines).  The output of the pager's
\fBannotations\fR command is not parsed.  A missing or unreadable database is reported, not fatal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print only the counts: entries answered, deferred and open, in total and by AFFECTS OPCODES.
Nothing is written.
.TP
.B \-\-all
List every entry in the report, answered or not.
.TP
.BR \-\-json " " \fIPATH\fR
Write the machine-readable answers there (default: \fIanswers.json\fR beside the form).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-json
Do not write answers.json.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-annotations
Do not read the annotation database.
.SH FILES
.I docs/feedback/answers.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfeedback.py (1),
.BR winless (1)
